// Hand-authored from the `gh search prs --help` documented JSON field list (gh 2.x):
//   assignees, author, authorAssociation, body, closedAt, commentsCount, createdAt,
//   id, isDraft, isLocked, isPullRequest, labels, number, repository, state, title, updatedAt, url
// The repository sub-object shape (nameWithOwner carrying "owner/repo") follows gh's documented
// search output; Phase 9c live-reconciles both against real search output (the Phase-8 smoke's
// offline-iteration discipline — zero gh calls before then).
// Sample of: gh search prs --author @me --state open --limit 50
//            --json number,title,state,isDraft,labels,updatedAt,url,repository
// Shape notes (vs the repo-scoped `gh pr list`): rows span MULTIPLE repos — each carries a
// `repository` OBJECT whose `nameWithOwner` is the only key consumed; search's pr field list
// KEEPS `isDraft` but has no `reviewDecision` — the feed type carries no review verdicts.
// `state` arrives UPPERCASE ("OPEN"); `labels` is an array of label objects (only `name`
// consumed) or null; `updatedAt` is RFC 3339 or null. Rows: draft, mixed nameWithOwner values,
// empty labels, null updatedAt, null labels.
